message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Strange loop in J-space: self-description in a language-model feedback loop"
authors:
  - family-names: Tomasik
    given-names: Wiktor
date-released: 2026-10-19
version: "4.0.2"
url: "https://github.com/Pixedar/jspace-strange-loop"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Pixedar/jspace-strange-loop"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
keywords:
  - self-modeling
  - strange loop
  - language models
  - attention
  - representation geometry
  - multimodal models
abstract: >-
  A learned reader repeatedly summarizes a frozen language model's activity. Its summary
  sets the control state that determines the next reading. A centered-field objective
  trains the summary to distinguish possible updates after removing their common
  destination. Some runs develop substantial state dependence; path interventions
  locate most of it in feedback through the reader. Applying the reader's attention
  inside the language model changes predictions, but feedback through model processing
  remains weak. Predictions match response patterns while retaining large scale errors.
  The repository includes frozen J-space feedback, memory between reasoning segments,
  evidence selection, multimodal input experiments and their controls.
